From: zabeelbasheer <53309631+zabeelbasheer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:44:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: phase 3, mentor flow (per-gap coaching, action items,
 checklist persistence)

Bounded to one diagnostic question and one answer per red/amber
criterion, matching mentor_agent.py's own documented 3-step design,
not an open-ended chat per gap. Action items accumulate through the
session and are saved via save_checklist_items each round, since it
replaces the full list rather than appending. Mentor conversation
turns themselves aren't persisted, only the resulting action items.

Also applies the same JSON-mode + low-reasoning-effort fix from
evaluator.py to mentor_agent.py's three Groq calls, generate_action_item
had the identical latent parsing risk with gpt-oss-120b before this.

due_days from the LLM is now converted into an actual due_date before
saving, it was being generated and silently discarded.
